s to sun-swept valleys  then there are enclosed areas which you  can only travel to via the games map  we've seen two of them firstly the Royal  Palace in vizima and secondly the home  of the witch's care [ __ ] which exists  to the far north of the main map there  could be more of these and we couldn't  travel to care more in during our time  but we did learn that you'll be fighting  alongside other witches there later in  the game and that's to say nothing of  the story beats with ciri the games  other playable character but we'll get  to those in the next video you're also  free to return to the prologue area of  the game and anytime to complete any  remaining side quests explore the world  or simply get in a fistfight with the  local cops  of course this is just what exists in  the immortal realm  CD Projekt are hiding some of the more  fantastical places up their sleeves I  don't really want to spoil this story  okay but there are certain places there  are places in the world that you will  you will come across this quite  non-natural and odd-looking definitely  so let's talk about the Maine open world  first of all it's bloody big I attempted  to run from the center of the map all  the way to novigrad and its northern  limit and even that took me about 20  minutes on horseback but granted I  probably didn't take the most direct  route mostly because the land here is  more dense than a lot of other open  worlds villages are numerous and packed  tightly together each with its own  message board full of side quests and  stories and as you wander into these new  villages there signposts become new fast  travel locations you ride with your  horse you stop and you see something's  over there you want to go there you want  to explore and see what you can find  them maybe you come across a village on  the way maybe there's a monster hunting  quest so it's all this kind of things  just happens and this is what we wanted  to have with the game where when you  explore the overworld apparently  everyone in the village has their own  routines and schedules from sunrise to  sunset unless of course it starts  raining we have lots of different types  of weather of course but important thing  to note this is not only cosmetic effect  it actually has an effect on community  so you know there were all rains I  better find shelter  you know it's nighttime people pack up  their things from the markets square and  go home but also monsters some monsters  are affected by the weather so when you  go monster hunting depending on the  monster you have to pay attention to  what time of day it is but the world of  The Witcher 3 isn't all just rolling  hills and swamps the vast city of  novigrad lies to the north with boats  bars and brothels for you to enjoy it's  a bustling vibrant city full of life and  from the sound of things we're gonna be  spending a lot of time there novigrad  isn't as large as say the cities and  Assassin's Creed but it's detail it's  quite impressive  streets packed with citizens bustling  bars and brothels you can wander into it  at a single loading screen walking into  novigrad is one of those times that the  witcher's technical prowess is on full  display hmm so one question you guys  keep asking us is how does this look on  console it's obviously when we went and  played the game we were playing the PC  version as you can see from the trailers  and the 4k screenshots looks pretty  great yeah but while we're at set a  project red we  she got a little sneak peek at the  console versions at Oh PS for an Xbox  one in this room where they were testing  performance for those versions you so  set it up for visual parodies  that's incredible yes we played a bit  six hours of the PC version yeah that's  great to see those are they look  fantastic  excellent on ps4 was it wonderful they  were sort of tweaking how it looked for  a frame rate optimisation while we were  there so a little bit of frame with  hitching obviously this 