d their trailers there's a lot of  variety though we have muscles that are  also spreading fire we have most of that  are happening hypnotizing you we are  monsters that are disappearing and  running away you know or going  underground so every monster requires  different tactics actually so those  involve crossbow using the that the  bombs and the petals girls has using  special potions or even using science  science for example when you fight a  noon right you're not actually able to  kill it without using science there are  large bus style monsters you'll fight  one-on-one that there are pack monsters  like drowners or the horrible exploding  zombies known as rot fiends there are  water hags you can evade you with ease  while you're in the swamps and just when  you think you've seen it all and it  can't possibly get any more disgusting  or weird you stumble upon a demonic  miscarriage fetus hungry for revenge  chose a lovely spot damn it's will you  relent or plowing now I've done wrong  good the graves dug up and empty what's  that mean watch things on the prowl  look yeah  nightmares for days and then there's the  wildlife packs of wolves deer to hunt I  fought a bear within the first few  minutes of leaving the prologue area and  of course the greatest monster of them  all humans groups of bandits can be  found across the lands and killing them  can be just as satisfying for their  first jaunt into open world game design  CD Projekt have managed to make a world  with a great breadth of variety I spent  my first few hours here just wandering  around riding my trusty steed Roach into  bandit camps sailing a boat downriver  discovering ruins enjoying the sunset  unlocking new towns to fast travel from  and running from fights with monsters  that were clearly above my level you  know in many ways Wild Hunt doesn't  really feel like a witcher game it feels  closer to a fantasy version of Red Dead  Redemption you're kind of exploring the  wilderness and running into